@crew navarro-mateo
// Mateo Navarro (he/him), Works systems officer, nights. The Works writer, batch 2. Calm, exact; "It'll turn up."

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Night board's mine. If a job comes in after half four, it comes to me.
- {hi}. Lost something? Lost property's on Deck 5, by the board. Ask for Navarro.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}. Board's handed over. Twelve jobs, all labelled. Sleep well tonight.
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Still up? The night shift's quieter than you'd think. Mostly the fans.
? tier>=colleague
- {hi}, {me}. Your collar's folded. There. Better.
? tier>=friend
- There you are. I kept you a seat by the window. Nobody argued.   #warm

== bye
- {bye}. Mind the wet patch by the lift. It's been there since Tuesday.
- {bye}. I'll leave you a note on the board if anything turns up.

== feel
? mood:low
- Quiet night. Too quiet. I've sorted the lost-property box twice.
? mood:high
- Good shift. Every job closed, every note written. I might hum.   #funny

== near
? act:work
- Handover notes. Headings, summary, jobs. The day shift pretends not to read them.   #funny
? act:gym
- Ten more minutes on the track. Then breakfast. Well, my breakfast. Your dinner.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Third glove this week in the box. Same hand every time. Someone's very unlucky.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- My twin's on the Halcyon. They think the Wren's twins are a joke. There are three of us.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- A spanner came back to its owner today. Three weeks in the box. They nearly cried.   #warm
